---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site.js";
const updated = "August 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service and Engagement | Kool Konsulting IN"
  description="The terms on which Kool Konsulting provides consulting services: scope, fees, cancellation, ownership of work, confidentiality, guarantees and liability limits."
  path="/terms"
  ogSlug="terms"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Terms", href: "/terms" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <p class="label label-accent">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="t-display" style="margin-top:1rem;">Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="form-note" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <p>
          These terms apply to consulting services provided by {SITE.name}. Each
          engagement also has its own written scope, and where the two differ the
          scope document takes precedence.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Scope of work</h2>
        <p>
          Before any work begins we agree a written scope setting out what will be
          delivered, the timeline and the fee. Anything outside that scope is quoted
          separately and started only once you have agreed it in writing. We will not
          run up a bill on work you did not ask for.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Fees and payment</h2>
        <p>
          One-off engagements are billed half on starting and half on delivery.
          Monthly services are invoiced in advance. All fees exclude GST, which is
          added at the prevailing rate. Advertising spend, hosting and third-party
          subscriptions are paid by you directly to those providers and are not
          marked up by us. Invoices are due within fourteen days.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Cancellation</h2>
        <p>
          If work has not started, any advance is returned in full. If work is under
          way, either side may end the engagement with thirty days' written notice;
          you pay for work completed to that date and we deliver everything produced
          so far. Monthly services carry a three-month minimum term.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          On payment in full, you own everything produced for you — source code,
          documents, financial models, campaign assets and account access. Code is
          delivered to a repository in your name. We retain ownership of our own
          pre-existing tools, templates and methods, and may reuse general knowledge
          and techniques gained during the engagement.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to provide accurate information, timely access to accounts and
          systems we need, and decisions within the timeframes agreed. Delays in
          these move the delivery date and may affect the fee where they cause
          material rescheduling.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>
          We treat your business information as confidential and will not disclose it
          without your permission. We will not publish any case study, name you as a
          client or quote you without your written approval first.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">What we do not guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          We do not guarantee search rankings, enquiry volumes, revenue outcomes, loan
          approval or investment. These depend on factors outside our control,
          including competitor activity, search engine changes and third-party credit
          decisions. Any figures discussed are estimates based on stated assumptions
          and are not promises. We commit to performing the agreed work competently
          and to reporting results honestly, including when they are poor.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Liability</h2>
        <p>
          Our total liability arising from an engagement is limited to the fees paid
          for that engagement. Neither party is liable for indirect or consequential
          loss, including lost profits. Nothing here limits liability for fraud or for
          anything that cannot lawfully be limited.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at Nagpur,
          Maharashtra have exclusive jurisdiction. We will attempt in good faith to
          resolve any dispute by discussion before either side commences proceedings.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-title">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 46rem; }
  .legal .prose h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 0.9rem; }
  .legal .prose a { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
